or geostationary, medium, and low earth orbit. The company also provides in-flight connectivity, narrowband safety operational data, and other complementary services; multimedia connectivity for military and government; tactical and beyond-line-of-sight communications; intelligence surveillance and reconnaissance; L-band advanced communications element terminals; enterprise connectivity solutions; Internet-of-Things; and L-band managed, energy, and prepaid internet services. In addition, it offers networking, cybersecurity, and information assurance products and services; high assurance internet protocol encryption solutions; MOJO expeditionary tactical gateway; government satellite communication systems, mobile and fixed broadband modems, ground and airborne terminals, antennas and gateways, Ka-band earth stations, and other multi-band/multi-function antennas, as well as design products for manpacks, aircraft, unmanned aerial vehicles, seagoing vessels, ground-mobile vehicles, space-based systems, and fixed applications. Further, the company designs and develops GEO, LEO, and MEO satellites, payload, antenna technologies, and other small satellite platforms; develops commercial communication satellite product, orchestration of sovereign and multi-orbit solutions, and direct-to-device; and licenses intellectual property. Viasat, Inc. was incorporated in 1986 and is headquartered in Carlsbad, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark D. Dankberg | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 70 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $663K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["ViaSat, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $8.8B market cap on $4.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at -10.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 35% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Viasat Inc (VSAT) Q2 2027 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/viasat-inc-vsat-q2-2027-081439000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793953717.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.064,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Is Viasat (VSAT) In Focus Over Takeover Talk And Spectrum Pushback?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-vsat/viasat/news/why-is-viasat-vsat-in-focus-over-takeover-talk-and-spectrum","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793949993.756,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Viasat Inc (VSAT) (Q2 2027) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Defense Growth and Satellite ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/viasat-inc-vsat-q2-2027-052936709.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793942976.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Viasat expects more than $225M free cash flow in fiscal 2027 while cutting capex to $850M-$900M (NASDAQ:VSAT)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667652-viasat-expects-more-than-225m-free-cash-flow-in-fiscal-2027-while-cutting-capex-to-850m-900m","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793930829.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.703,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ViaSat (VSAT) Q2 Earnings: Taking a Look at Key Metrics Versus Estimates","sourc