 the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 31% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 82% and a beta of 1.05, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 2.89 vs 5y 1.16), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $127.5M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 63% in the 2020 crash, 49% in the 2022 bear market and 54% in 2008."],"val":["Multiples send mixed signals against Technology peers: cheaper on EV/EBITDA 9.9 vs 16.4, richer on P/E 383.7 vs 26.7 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 35% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 0.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 10 covering analysts target $104 on average, 63% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 1% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value.","Earnings quality is a concern: high accruals (-10.7% of assets).","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 3.6% of revenue on R&D and 1.7% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.1x net debt to EBITDA ($1.7B of cash against $6.4B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 0.3x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.94 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The value-trap profile is elevated (51/100); see the breakdown below.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.41)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 22.0% over 3 years, 15.5% over 5 years and 11.5% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.11 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 88% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 26%.","Capex runs 2.6x depreciation (42.1% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.9%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (9 sales, net $1.7M sold).","The share count has grown 14.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 10.2% of the float, 6.2 days to cover."],"people":["With about 7,000 employees, each generates about $663K of revenue, 1.8x the Technology median, and productivity has risen 11.6% a year.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $3.9M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $12K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"VSAT","date":"2026-11-06"}